ffmpeg-tiny is an independent package using FFmpeg's libavcodec and libavutil.
FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard. This package is not an official
FFmpeg distribution or an endorsement by the FFmpeg project.

FFmpeg and this package's source are distributed under LGPL-2.1-or-later.
See LICENSE. The build excludes GPL and nonfree components.

The exact, unmodified FFmpeg source is included in dist/ffmpeg-source.tar.gz.
The C shim and JavaScript wrapper source, compiler pin and build instructions
are included so recipients can rebuild and replace the decoder. FFmpeg's
individual source files retain their original copyright and license notices.

The generated runtime also uses Emscripten and musl libc. Their notices and
license texts are included in dist/licenses/. FFmpeg's source archive contains
additional upstream tools and optional components under their own licenses;
they are not all part of the decoder binary.
